From 35f4a42d6c999bd7e53bd40ba3ffac63489859a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:39:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Swap in a turntable video below desktop instead of the live
 model
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Even deferred to an explicit tap, decompressing this model was still
enough to crash the tab on phones that tried it. Below this site's
desktop breakpoint (1180px), a pre-rendered 360 turntable video now
replaces <model-viewer> whenever one is set on the block —
mobileFallbackVideo, a new optional upload field — so there is nothing
for a phone's GPU to choke on: the viewer isn't mounted there at all,
not de-prioritised. The isDesktop check starts false and only flips
true once matchMedia has explicitly confirmed a desktop width, because
the failure mode that matters is a phone briefly mounting the viewer
before JS corrects it, not a desktop reader seeing the video for a
frame. Without a fallback video set, behaviour on mobile/tablet is
unchanged from before this patch (interactive viewer, tap to load).

Database: 20261002_130000_add_model_3d_mobile_fallback_video is a
second, separate migration (ALTER TABLE, not a rewrite of the first
one's CREATE TABLE) — 20261002_120000_add_model_3d_block had already
run against the live database by the time this field existed.
